It&#x27;s touted by the people who use the word &quot;just&quot; a lot.<p>&quot;Just use postgres&quot;
&quot;Just use sqlite&quot;
&quot;Juse use a monolith&quot;
&quot;Just use sftp&quot;
&quot;Just use an ec2 instance&quot;<p>Usually these people have flunked out of the school of (distributed system) hard knocks. They couldn&#x27;t hack it and are retreating to familiar.<p>The funny part is when one of those people fluke themselves into senior management when their saas takes off.<p>Inevitably they have to suck it up and hire experts in the same technologies that &quot;no one needs&quot;.
